      "id": "notebook-introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Notebook introduction"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "This document provides an exhaustive technical breakdown of the **`firstInstance` bit-packing architecture**, its role in bindless state dispatching, mathematical limits, hardware instancing mechanics, pass discrimination, and safeguards in the Retiam WebGPU Engine."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1-executive-summary-core-architectural-role",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "1. Executive Summary & Core Architectural Role"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "In WebGPU, `firstInstance` is the parameter passed to draw commands:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "`pass.draw(vertexCount, instanceCount, firstVertex, firstInstance)`",
            "`pass.drawIndexed(indexCount, instanceCount, firstIndex, baseVertex, firstInstance)`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "The WebGPU Built-In Behavior:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "When a draw call executes on the GPU, the vertex shader receives the built-in variable `@builtin(instance_index)`. The GPU automatically computes:"
        },
        {
          "type": "math",
          "tex": "\\text{instance\\_index} = \\text{firstInstance} + i \\quad \\text{where } i \\in [0, \\text{instanceCount} - 1]"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "Why Retiam Bit-Packs firstInstance:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "In traditional rendering engines, `firstInstance` is simply used as an offset ($0, 1, 2 \\dots$). However, in Retiam's **Zero-GC Bindless Architecture**, `firstInstance` is repurposed as a **high-density 32-bit multiplexer** that carries:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "items": [
            "**Bindless Entity State Index** (`state_index`): Points directly to `states[state_index]` in `@group(2) @binding(0)` (transform matrices, paint colors, clipping bounds).",
            "**Local Instance Index** (`local_index`): Offsets into per-entity storage buffers (e.g. `instances[local_index * 3]`).",
            "**Pass Discrimination Flag** (`isStroke`): Dispatches Fill vs. Stroke sub-passes through an uber-shader in a single draw call.",
            "**Mode Switch (Bit 31)**: Dynamically expands instance capacity from 16k to 262k objects without shader recompilation."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "mermaid",
          "code": "flowchart TD\n    A[\"pass.draw / pass.drawIndexed(..., firstInstance)\"] --> B[\"WebGPU Built-in: instance_index = firstInstance + i\"]\n    B --> C{\"Bit 31 Mode Switch\"}\n    \n    C -->|\"Bit 31 = 0 (Standard Mode)\"| D[\"getStateIndex: Bits 29..14 (0..65,535)<br/>getLocalIndex: Bits 13..0 (0..16,383)\"]\n    C -->|\"Bit 31 = 1 (Mega Mode)\"| E[\"getStateIndex: Bits 29..18 (0..4,095)<br/>getLocalIndex: Bits 17..0 (0..262,143)\"]\n    \n    B --> F[\"getIsStroke: Bit 30 (0x40000000)<br/>0 = Fill Pass, 1 = Stroke Pass\"]\n    \n    D --> G[\"Lookup states[state_index] in @group(2)\"]\n    E --> G\n    D --> H[\"Pull instances[local_index] in @group(3)\"]\n    E --> H\n    F --> I[\"Uber-Shader Branchless Fill/Stroke Evaluation\"]"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2-dual-mode-32-bit-allocation-layout",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "2. Dual-Mode 32-Bit Allocation Layout"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The 32-bit unsigned integer `instance_index` is partitioned into two mutually exclusive packing schemes determined by the Most Significant Bit (Bit 31):"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "columns": [
