    },
    {
      "id": "3-typescript-encoder-wgsl-branchless-decoder",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "3. TypeScript Encoder & WGSL Branchless Decoder"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "TypeScript Encoder ([src/engine/utils/gpuutils.ts](../src/engine/utils/gpuutils.ts#L162-L182)):"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "typescript",
          "code": "/**\n * Packs a state index, local instance index, and pass flag into a 32-bit instance_index.\n * - Bit 31: Mode switch (0 = Standard, 1 = Mega-Instance)\n * - Bit 30: Secondary / Stroke flag (0 = Fill / Default, 1 = Stroke)\n * - Mode 0 (Standard, MSB = 0): 16-bit state (0..65,535), 14-bit local index (0..16,383)\n * - Mode 1 (Mega-Instance, MSB = 1): 12-bit state (0..4,095), 18-bit local index (0..262,143)\n */\nexport function packInstanceIndex(\n    stateIndex: number,\n    localIndex: number = 0,\n    isMega: boolean = false,\n    isStroke: boolean = false\n): number {\n    const strokeBit = isStroke ? 0x40000000 : 0;\n    if (isMega || localIndex > 16383) {\n        return (0x80000000 | strokeBit | ((stateIndex & 0xFFF) << 18) | (localIndex & 0x3FFFF)) >>> 0;\n    }\n    return (strokeBit | ((stateIndex & 0xFFFF) << 14) | (localIndex & 0x3FFF)) >>> 0;\n}"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "Branchless WGSL Decoder ([src/engine/shaders/includes/common.wgsl](../src/engine/shaders/includes/common.wgsl#L103-L115)):"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "wgsl",
          "code": "fn getStateIndex(instance_index: u32) -> u32 {\n    let is_mega = (instance_index & 0x80000000u) != 0u;\n    return select((instance_index >> 14u) & 0xFFFFu, (instance_index >> 18u) & 0xFFFu, is_mega);\n}\n\nfn getLocalIndex(instance_index: u32) -> u32 {\n    let is_mega = (instance_index & 0x80000000u) != 0u;\n    return select(instance_index & 0x3FFFu, instance_index & 0x3FFFFu, is_mega);\n}\n\nfn getIsStroke(instance_index: u32) -> bool {\n    return (instance_index & 0x40000000u) != 0u;\n}"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "Why Branchless select() Matters:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "In WGSL, `select(falseVal, trueVal, condition)` compiles directly into a single GPU hardware conditional move (`csel` / `movc`). There is **zero branch divergence**, zero warp stalling, and zero penalty across adjacent GPU execution threads."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4-hardware-instancing-arithmetic-carry-rollovers",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "4. Hardware Instancing Arithmetic & Carry Rollovers"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "The Mathematical Vulnerability:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "When WebGPU runs hardware instancing, it increments the index for each instance:"
        },
        {
          "type": "math",
          "tex": "\\text{instance\\_index}_i = \\text{firstInstance} + i \\quad (i = 0, 1, 2 \\dots \\text{instanceCount}-1)"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "In binary addition:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "In Mode 0, `localIndex` occupies Bits 0..13 (max value $2^{14}-1 = 16,383$).",
            "If an entity starts at `localStart = 10,000` and draws `instanceCount = 10,000`, the final instance reaches $i = 19,999$.",
            "In binary, $16,384 = \\text{0x4000} = (1 \\ll 14)$.",
            "**Addition Carry**: Adding past 16,383 carries a $+1$ directly into **Bit 14** (the lowest bit of `stateIndex`)!",
            "**Consequence**: The GPU starts reading state transforms from $(\\text{stateIndex} + 1)$—a completely different entity in the scene, causing tearing and transform corruption."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "The Engine Solution (Total Span Validation):"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "All Retiam renderers calculate `isMega` by checking the **total instance span**, not just `instanceCount`:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "typescript",
          "code": "const localStart = call.firstInstance ?? 0;\nconst isMega = (localStart + (call.instanceCount || 1)) > 16384;\nconst firstInstance = packInstanceIndex(stateIndex, localStart, isMega, call.isStroke ?? false);"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "When the total span exceeds 16,384:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "items": [
            "`packInstanceIndex` switches to Mode 1.",
            "Bit 31 is set to `1`.",
            "`localIndex` bit-width expands from 14 bits to **18 bits** (up to **262,143 instances**).",
            "Binary addition carries cannot reach Bit 18 until $i \\ge 262,144$, completely preventing state corruption."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5-pass-discrimination-the-bit-30-revolution",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "5. Pass Discrimination & The Bit 30 Revolution"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "The Legacy Problem (Bit 0):"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Previously, some shaders attempted to differentiate fill and stroke by using the least significant bit (`instance_index & 1u`)."
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "In single-draw mode: Draw Call 0 had `firstInstance = 0` (even = Fill), Draw Call 1 had `firstInstance = 1` (odd = Stroke).",
            "**Failure Under Instancing**: When rendering 1,000 instances of a path, instance $0$ was even (Fill), instance $1$ was odd (Stroke), instance $2$ was even (Fill)... Every adjacent instance inverted its visual styling!"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "The Bit 30 Solution:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "By reserving **Bit 30 (`0x40000000`)** exclusively as the `isStroke` flag:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "items": [
            "**Full Isolation**: Bit 30 is 16 bits above the Mode 0 local index boundary and 12 bits above the Mode 1 local index boundary. Hardware instance additions $0..262,143$ can **never** flip Bit 30.",
            "**Fill Execution**: Fill draw call issues `firstInstance` with Bit 30 = 0. All $N$ instances render with fill.",
            "**Stroke Execution**: Stroke draw call issues `firstInstance` with Bit 30 = 1. All $N$ instances render with stroke.",
            "**2 Draw Calls for $N$ Vector Paths**: 50,000 vector shapes render fill and stroke in exactly 2 draw calls with zero style flipping."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
